WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:03.920
WRITTEN BY HYUGA NATSU

01:34.886 --> 01:36.137
This caravan...

01:36.721 --> 01:39.516
has so many merchants
and such a variety of goods.

01:40.016 --> 01:42.852
It’s the advance party
for welcoming foreign envoys.

01:42.936 --> 01:45.188
I heard it’s larger than usual...

01:45.271 --> 01:47.816
and expected to last longer than usual.

01:48.316 --> 01:49.776
How are the banquet preparations?

01:50.610 --> 01:53.488
Senior officials in charge
are handling it.

01:53.571 --> 01:54.739
I see.

01:55.448 --> 01:58.118
They’re important guests.
Keep up the work.

01:58.993 --> 01:59.953
Understood.

02:02.455 --> 02:04.791
The humidity’s been increasing, so...

02:04.874 --> 02:07.127
I think it’s time to
switch to seasonal attire.

02:07.710 --> 02:09.712
First, I’ll organize my wardrobe.

02:09.796 --> 02:12.549
Yinghua, Ailan, Maomao.

02:12.632 --> 02:14.634
- Yes.
- Yes, Miss Hongniang.

02:15.426 --> 02:18.012
Guiyuan, please take care of
Princess Lingli.

02:18.096 --> 02:19.139
Understood.

02:21.933 --> 02:24.978
There are quite a few outdated designs.

02:25.061 --> 02:27.647
This one might still work.

02:28.690 --> 02:31.860
This one was really popular
for a while, but...

02:31.943 --> 02:33.111
with trendy things,

02:33.194 --> 02:36.364
once the trend passes,
they suddenly become useless.

02:38.199 --> 02:40.368
What will happen to the old ones?

02:40.451 --> 02:43.913
The craftsmen will remake them
and send them to Lady Gyokuyou's homeland.

02:43.997 --> 02:45.999
To the West.

02:46.082 --> 02:48.501
Then just to be safe...

02:48.585 --> 02:51.212
I'll put some insect-repelling
herbs in them.

02:51.296 --> 02:52.255
Yes, thank you.

02:52.338 --> 02:53.506
By the way,

02:53.590 --> 02:56.259
a new attendant will be coming soon.

02:57.051 --> 02:58.344
A new attendant?

02:59.178 --> 03:00.847
<i>Because of Lady Gyokuyou's pregnancy,</i>

03:01.431 --> 03:04.309
<i>we'll need even more help.</i>

03:04.809 --> 03:07.395
There are other reasons too.

03:07.478 --> 03:09.731
With over 50 attendants
and servants at her side,

03:09.814 --> 03:12.150
there is a consort who entered the court.

03:12.650 --> 03:14.777
So of course Lady Gyokuyou needs more.

03:14.861 --> 03:16.154
<i>Is this about Lady Loulan?</i>

03:17.071 --> 03:20.033
<i>It’s true, Lady Gyokuyou,
the Emperor's primary consort</i>

03:20.116 --> 03:23.036
<i>only has five attendants,
and it looks bad.</i>

03:23.703 --> 03:26.247
Even Lady Lihua of the Crystal Pavilion

03:26.331 --> 03:28.416
only has 30 servants, including maids.

03:28.499 --> 03:31.377
But the Garnet Pavilion has twice that!
Isn’t that strange?

03:31.961 --> 03:34.255
Yinghua, if you say things like that,

03:34.339 --> 03:36.758
you’ll get scolded
by Miss Hongniang again.

03:36.841 --> 03:37.884
But it’s true!

03:38.468 --> 03:40.011
Well then,

03:40.094 --> 03:42.180
it's looking much cleaner now.

03:42.263 --> 03:44.307
Is it really okay to reduce this much?

03:44.390 --> 03:45.350
Don’t worry.

03:45.433 --> 03:47.977
I’ve ordered a few new wardrobes.

03:48.061 --> 03:50.897
And the caravan will be here soon!

03:51.648 --> 03:52.523
Caravan?

03:52.607 --> 03:56.194
Last time it came,
you weren’t around, Maomao.

03:57.028 --> 04:00.406
<i>This time, it’s much larger than usual!</i>

04:00.990 --> 04:03.451
<i>It’s not that unusual
in the pleasure district,</i>

04:03.534 --> 04:05.453
<i>but in the rear palace
where fun is scarce,</i>

04:05.536 --> 04:08.414
<i>shopping like this is something
they all look forward to.</i>

04:08.498 --> 04:12.168
Maomao, make some free time and go see it.

04:12.252 --> 04:13.419
Lady Gyokuyou,

04:13.503 --> 04:16.172
always gives me pocket money
at times like this--

04:16.256 --> 04:17.548
Oh, what’s wrong?

04:19.509 --> 04:23.763
Stop chatting and get to work!

04:26.349 --> 04:30.436
I have to be careful too,
or Hongniang will scold me.

04:30.520 --> 04:33.815
Lady Gyokuyou, please stop with the jokes.

04:50.248 --> 04:52.667
Have you called for me, Lady Lihua?

04:53.251 --> 04:55.712
Shin, take this to everyone.

04:57.922 --> 05:00.216
Is this for the caravan shopping?

05:00.300 --> 05:03.094
I’ll have one of the free maids go buy it.

05:03.678 --> 05:05.138
Yes, please.

05:20.111 --> 05:23.740
Lady Shin. A message from the clinic.

05:24.615 --> 05:26.326
A message from the clinic?

05:34.334 --> 05:37.128
<i>The caravan will stay for five days.</i>

05:40.840 --> 05:43.217
<i>With the consorts
and their attendants having fun,</i>

05:43.301 --> 05:46.679
<i>there’s no way the lower-ranked servants
can join in and shop.</i>

05:46.763 --> 05:48.514
How nice!

05:48.598 --> 05:51.642
I want new clothes too.

05:51.726 --> 05:53.102
Though you can't wear them.

05:53.186 --> 05:54.729
I know, but I still want them!

05:56.064 --> 05:57.523
<i>The rear palace.</i>

05:57.607 --> 05:59.942
<i>It’s a very unique place.</i>

06:00.026 --> 06:02.695
<i>There are so many people, but no stores,</i>

06:02.779 --> 06:05.490
<i>and the only doctor is Quack Doctor.</i>

06:06.074 --> 06:09.535
<i>Some may believe that
if anyone got sick, it’d spread quickly,</i>

06:09.619 --> 06:10.912
<i>but that’s not the case.</i>

06:10.995 --> 06:13.456
<i>The hygiene management is strict.</i>

06:14.165 --> 06:16.084
<i>The sewage system flows underground,</i>

06:16.167 --> 06:18.961
<i>connecting to the great river,
without passing through a moat.</i>

06:19.545 --> 06:23.424
<i>Empress Dowager, known for her skill,
utilized Western waterways techniques.</i>

06:24.217 --> 06:28.513
<i>If hygiene is managed properly,
diseases can be prevented.</i>

06:28.596 --> 06:29.514
<i>Still...</i>

06:29.597 --> 06:32.600
<i>if someone falls seriously ill,
they’re sent back to their family...</i>

06:32.683 --> 06:34.310
Hey, Maomao.

06:36.312 --> 06:37.897
On the last day,

06:37.980 --> 06:40.900
I might be able to get a bit of free time...

06:43.945 --> 06:46.155
<i>I wouldn’t mind being invited.</i>

06:54.747 --> 06:56.833
Did I overspend a bit?

06:57.416 --> 07:00.753
Not at all, you could’ve bought even more.

07:00.837 --> 07:03.506
Others are probably buying
much more than us.

07:04.173 --> 07:05.007
<i>Indeed.</i>

07:05.842 --> 07:09.804
<i>The attendants of the Crystal Pavilion
tend to shop extravagantly,</i>

07:09.887 --> 07:12.265
<i>and Lady Lihua is quite generous
despite everything.</i>

07:12.932 --> 07:15.852
<i>At the Diamond Pavilion,
Lady Lishu’s attendants</i>

07:15.935 --> 07:19.021
<i>might sweet-talk her
into buying whatever they want.</i>

07:19.814 --> 07:21.190
<i>At the Garnet Pavilion,</i>

07:21.274 --> 07:24.193
<i>Lady Loulan's love for extravagance
goes without saying.</i>

07:25.194 --> 07:28.781
<i>In contrast, Lady Gyokuyou is frugal,
fitting everything into one room.</i>

07:29.282 --> 07:31.701
The caravan merchants
will be back tomorrow,

07:31.784 --> 07:33.703
so let’s tidy up today’s purchases.

07:33.786 --> 07:35.037
Got it.

07:39.083 --> 07:40.001
<i>Huh?</i>

07:41.043 --> 07:41.961
What’s wrong?

07:43.171 --> 07:44.881
<i>Most of these outfits have sleeves,</i>

07:44.964 --> 07:47.925
<i>and a skirt tied with
a sash right under the chest.</i>

07:48.801 --> 07:51.262
Were there no other types of clothing?

07:51.345 --> 07:53.181
Nope, it was all the same.

07:53.264 --> 07:55.975
They said it’s trendy.

07:58.561 --> 08:02.190
<i>Lady Gyokuyou’s pregnancy
is still a secret.</i>

08:02.899 --> 08:06.569
<i>Normally, merchants bring outfits
that appeal to their customers.</i>

08:06.652 --> 08:10.114
<i>For Lady Gyokuyou, they’d choose
sashes tied at the waist.</i>

08:10.198 --> 08:12.825
<i>But as her belly grows,</i>

08:12.909 --> 08:14.952
<i>she’d prefer loose-fitting clothing.</i>

08:15.745 --> 08:17.622
<i>Considering that,</i>

08:17.705 --> 08:21.542
<i>if they deliberately
brought these designs...</i>

08:22.043 --> 08:24.504
<i>I’d like to think
I’m overthinking it, but...</i>

08:27.089 --> 08:31.052
Tomorrow, we should ask
if they have designs

08:31.135 --> 08:32.845
with sashes tied securely at the waist.

08:35.806 --> 08:36.807
You’re right.

08:37.475 --> 08:39.769
We need to buy something different.

08:40.728 --> 08:43.689
Hongniang, notify the merchants.

08:43.773 --> 08:44.982
Understood.

08:46.067 --> 08:49.153
<i>It seems Lady Gyokuyou
and Miss Hongniang understand.</i>

08:54.242 --> 08:57.161
<i>On the last day,
all that’s left are the leftovers...</i>

08:58.454 --> 09:00.873
Wow, amazing!

09:08.798 --> 09:12.009
<i>Lady Gyokuyou gave me
some pocket money, but...</i>

09:15.179 --> 09:16.305
Please give me this.

09:18.849 --> 09:20.142
It suits you.

09:24.397 --> 09:27.191
Thanks, Maomao!

09:27.275 --> 09:31.279
<i>If I had a younger sister,
she might be like this little creature.</i>

09:31.862 --> 09:34.991
Maomao, is there anywhere you want to go?
I’ll come with you.

09:35.658 --> 09:38.995
Then, there’s a place
I’d like to take a quick look at.

09:41.581 --> 09:44.000
<i>Of course, there aren’t any medicines,</i>

09:44.083 --> 09:46.419
<i>but they do have tea leaves and spices.</i>

09:47.587 --> 09:51.424
<i>And there’s one more reason
I came on the last day...</i>

09:52.174 --> 09:53.676
<i>Discounts.</i>

09:54.260 --> 09:56.053
<i>In a unique place like the rear palace,</i>

09:56.137 --> 09:58.973
<i>it’s hard to imagine
they’d sell goods at fair prices.</i>

09:59.056 --> 10:01.601
<i>Don’t think you can
overcharge me so easily.</i>

10:21.162 --> 10:22.663
<i>Jasmine tea, huh?</i>

10:23.956 --> 10:25.082
Please give me this.

10:28.711 --> 10:30.379
Is the kitty doing well?

10:31.881 --> 10:33.090
<i>She's that girl from before...</i>

10:34.592 --> 10:37.178
He's doing well.
He's in the medical office now.

10:37.261 --> 10:38.929
I see. Glad to hear that!

10:39.513 --> 10:42.266
Huh? Did you get the day off too, Shisui?

10:42.350 --> 10:46.228
Yeah. You came too? What did you buy?

10:46.312 --> 10:48.147
I just came to look.

10:48.898 --> 10:53.194
- But Maomao bought me a hair tie!
- It’s so cute!

10:53.944 --> 10:55.655
<i>Do they know each other?</i>

10:55.738 --> 10:59.158
<i>Since she's wearing
the same robe as Xiaolan,</i>

10:59.241 --> 11:02.119
<i>she must be one of the ladies
who uses the usual laundry.</i>

11:03.204 --> 11:05.790
We're in the way,
so let’s move to another spot.

11:06.540 --> 11:07.875
Please give me three of these.

11:09.460 --> 11:12.755
I didn’t know you had friends, miss.

11:13.381 --> 11:15.800
<i>The quack doctor may be rude,</i>

11:15.883 --> 11:18.761
<i>but it’s the truth,
so there’s nothing to be done about it.</i>

11:18.844 --> 11:20.054
MAOMAO

11:20.638 --> 11:21.972
So cute!

11:22.056 --> 11:23.599
What’s its name?

11:23.682 --> 11:24.809
Rat Exterminator.

11:24.892 --> 11:27.269
Huh? That’s a weird name.

11:27.937 --> 11:30.773
<i>The name Maomao is way weirder.</i>

11:31.357 --> 11:32.858
Shall I make some tea?

11:32.942 --> 11:34.443
I’ve brought tea.

11:35.027 --> 11:36.862
Then let’s have some sweets.

11:49.708 --> 11:51.585
It smells nice.

11:51.669 --> 11:53.170
It's jasmine flowering tea.

11:53.796 --> 11:55.548
You place it in a warmed pot,

11:55.631 --> 11:59.176
and slowly pour in lukewarm water
like this, and the buds open up.

11:59.260 --> 12:02.138
It’s not often that you get a chance
to brew it like this.

12:02.221 --> 12:05.766
Girls, here's a special treat.

12:05.850 --> 12:08.936
Mooncakes! Thank you very much.

12:11.605 --> 12:14.024
By the way, is it always like this?

12:14.108 --> 12:15.985
Such a big celebration.

12:16.068 --> 12:18.946
<i>Is this her first time at the caravan?</i>

12:19.029 --> 12:21.866
<i>If she entered
with Lady Loulan’s marriage,</i>

12:21.949 --> 12:23.742
<i>she must have been here for half a year.</i>

12:25.786 --> 12:27.788
This time, it’s longer than usual.

12:27.872 --> 12:29.248
That’s because...

12:29.331 --> 12:32.793
it seems that a special envoy
from a foreign country is coming soon.

12:32.877 --> 12:35.379
Oh! A high-ranking person is coming, huh?

12:35.963 --> 12:38.340
<i>Is it okay to say that?</i>

12:38.424 --> 12:39.884
By the way,

12:39.967 --> 12:44.889
lately, there's a strange smell coming
from the north. Do you know about it?

12:45.473 --> 12:47.892
- The north?
- I don’t know.

12:47.975 --> 12:49.977
A strange smell, you say?

12:50.060 --> 12:54.231
That area is a mess.
Maybe the waterway is clogged.

12:54.315 --> 12:56.734
<i>If the underground channels
carrying waste gets clogged,</i>

12:56.817 --> 12:59.570
<i>the smell might rise to the surface.</i>

13:00.070 --> 13:02.406
Do you have any work in the northern area?

13:03.699 --> 13:05.993
That area has
a lot of grassy fields, right?

13:09.747 --> 13:10.581
You're good at drawing.

13:11.165 --> 13:15.920
Thanks. There's a lot of insects there,
so there's a lot to draw.

13:16.545 --> 13:19.673
<i>Insects can also be used as medicine.</i>

13:19.757 --> 13:24.094
<i>Mantis eggs are an energizer, and
earthworms have fever-reducing properties.</i>

13:24.845 --> 13:28.891
The southern orchard is well-maintained
so there aren’t many insects,

13:28.974 --> 13:31.310
but the northern ruins are a great place!

13:31.393 --> 13:33.229
There are a lot of big spiders!

13:33.312 --> 13:34.438
Spiders?

13:34.939 --> 13:37.983
It’s difficult to collect them
so I haven’t tried it yet,

13:38.067 --> 13:40.694
but spider silk is said to have
hemostatic properties.

13:40.778 --> 13:44.031
- Wanna go? Shall we try?
- Let’s go! Let’s try it.

13:44.114 --> 13:47.701
Look at this! It’s so beautiful and plump!
Isn’t it cute?

13:47.785 --> 13:49.703
They are delicious to eat
and you'll love them.

14:09.765 --> 14:11.600
<i>A few days after the caravan left...</i>

14:12.184 --> 14:15.437
<i>At the rear palace, fragrant oils
have become a huge trend.</i>

14:17.731 --> 14:19.191
It smells...

14:20.568 --> 14:21.986
It really stinks.

14:22.862 --> 14:25.406
<i>Imported products from the west
have strong scents.</i>

14:25.489 --> 14:27.157
<i>On their own, they smell good,</i>

14:27.241 --> 14:28.951
<i>but when mixed, they can be dangerous.</i>

14:31.453 --> 14:32.913
Ah, sorry!

14:35.958 --> 14:38.752
<i>Sniff, sniff. It’s rose.</i>

14:38.836 --> 14:42.840
<i>Maybe I could make a profit by
selling the rose water I made last time.</i>

14:43.507 --> 14:46.218
<i>No, the strong scent
of rose essential oil,</i>

14:46.302 --> 14:49.138
<i>could have a bad effect on pregnant women.</i>

14:49.221 --> 14:51.181
<i>In the current Jade Pavilion...</i>

14:57.021 --> 14:57.938
This smell...

15:08.741 --> 15:12.369
<i>I must go. To the Pavilion
most easily influenced by trends,</i>

15:12.453 --> 15:14.663
<i>the Crystal Pavilion!</i>

15:25.591 --> 15:27.968
You... what do you think you're doing?

15:30.846 --> 15:35.059
A protest letter has arrived from
the leader of the Crystal Pavilion, Shin.

15:35.768 --> 15:38.812
I thought you were a person
with more self-control.

15:38.896 --> 15:40.314
I’m sorry.

15:40.397 --> 15:44.401
I got carried away and did it
without even getting their consent.

15:44.485 --> 15:46.946
What kind of perverted excuse is that?

15:47.029 --> 15:49.823
- Next time, I'll smell it with your...
- Why smell it?!

15:49.907 --> 15:50.824
Oh dear.

15:54.370 --> 15:56.080
<i>That's enough for reflection, I guess.</i>

15:56.956 --> 15:58.457
But there is a reason for this.

15:59.166 --> 16:00.918
Is it a good enough reason?

16:02.127 --> 16:03.295
Yes.

16:04.713 --> 16:07.299
Lord Jinshi, could you please read

16:07.383 --> 16:09.301
what is written there?

16:09.385 --> 16:12.137
Okay. "Rose, benzoin,

16:12.221 --> 16:14.598
blue catalpa, frankincense, and cinnamon"?

16:15.182 --> 16:17.101
They all sound like
fragrance names, right?

16:17.184 --> 16:18.394
Yes.

16:18.894 --> 16:20.145
These are the names of

16:20.229 --> 16:23.190
the perfumes and oils that
the ladies wore that I smelled today.

16:23.774 --> 16:25.067
What about it?

16:25.567 --> 16:27.778
They are all harmful to pregnant women.

16:33.283 --> 16:34.535
Go on.

16:34.618 --> 16:36.662
Besides the perfumed oils,

16:36.745 --> 16:39.331
spices and tea leaves
were also sold at the caravan.

16:39.915 --> 16:42.167
These are the items I bought.

16:42.960 --> 16:46.797
Jasmine has the effect of
contracting the uterus.

16:46.880 --> 16:51.176
And poppy is often used as
an abortifacient for courtesans.

16:51.677 --> 16:56.598
In other words, using these could increase
the likelihood of a miscarriage?

16:56.682 --> 17:00.269
If it's in small quantities,
there should be no problems.

17:00.352 --> 17:03.856
As long as it's not taken in
large amounts or used incorrectly.

17:03.939 --> 17:07.109
<i>I should have noticed it earlier.</i>

17:07.192 --> 17:09.903
<i>Perhaps I was swept up
in the festive atmosphere.</i>

17:12.906 --> 17:15.200
Do you know the vendors
who supplied these?

17:15.284 --> 17:17.161
I can investigate,

17:17.661 --> 17:21.248
but they probably haven’t detailed
every product individually.

17:22.791 --> 17:25.377
I inspected everything I could.

17:27.463 --> 17:29.673
Doesn’t this resemble that?

17:29.757 --> 17:30.758
What is "that"?

17:31.425 --> 17:33.761
Something whose side effects
aren’t well known.

17:34.928 --> 17:37.306
It wouldn’t be surprising to find
it in the rear palace.

17:37.848 --> 17:41.602
Doesn’t it resemble the one
that harmed Princess Lingli,

17:41.685 --> 17:43.896
and caused the death of
Lady Lihua’s child?

17:44.646 --> 17:46.607
Poison... face powder.

17:49.485 --> 17:52.154
Yes, lead-based face powder.

17:53.489 --> 17:55.032
So, what this means is,

17:55.115 --> 17:58.243
someone attempted to
bring poison into the rear palace.

17:58.327 --> 17:59.453
Can we assume that?

18:00.662 --> 18:03.665
All I can say is that
many of the items that entered here

18:03.749 --> 18:07.377
could potentially be poisonous.

18:07.878 --> 18:11.215
None of them are considered
poisonous products by themselves.

18:11.965 --> 18:15.094
But, I think we should also be cautious
with the other consorts.

18:17.262 --> 18:19.556
- Gaoshun.
- Yes, Lord Jinshi.

18:20.766 --> 18:24.645
<i>It’s like the incident when coincidences
piled up and became inevitable.</i>

18:25.145 --> 18:28.315
- Hongniang, please.
- Yes, Lady Gyokuyou.

18:28.982 --> 18:29.858
Guiyuan,

18:29.942 --> 18:33.403
please check the oils, spices,
and tea leaves in the Jade Pavilion.

18:33.487 --> 18:34.321
Understood!

18:35.280 --> 18:37.908
<i>The palace attendant who revived
from a near-death state and fled,</i>

18:37.991 --> 18:41.411
<i>and the whereabouts of Suirei
are still unknown.</i>

18:45.666 --> 18:47.167
<i>For the assassination attempt
at the mid festival,</i>

18:47.709 --> 18:50.963
<i>it’s highly likely that
many people were involved.</i>

18:52.089 --> 18:55.008
<i>How far do their hands reach...?</i>

18:58.262 --> 19:01.849
<i>How much of it is speculation,
and how much of it is certainty?</i>

19:01.932 --> 19:04.935
You shouldn’t speak based on speculation.

19:10.566 --> 19:13.485
<i>If I wasn't assigned to the Consort’s
room, I would have lower salary</i>

19:13.569 --> 19:16.238
<i>and I probably wouldn’t have been
interested in the caravan.</i>

19:17.239 --> 19:20.576
<i>If the oils hadn’t become a trend,
I wouldn’t have noticed.</i>

19:21.076 --> 19:23.996
<i>Maybe this time was the only time
so many items were being sold.</i>

19:24.955 --> 19:28.584
Which part is coincidence,
and which is inevitability?

19:28.667 --> 19:30.752
I don’t even understand that...

19:34.131 --> 19:35.507
I’m tired...

19:37.926 --> 19:39.553
How nostalgic.

19:39.636 --> 19:41.305
Back in the day,
when there were no customers,

19:41.388 --> 19:45.017
the courtesans secretly let me drink it...

19:52.107 --> 19:54.610
Wasn’t that poison?

19:56.904 --> 20:00.199
Poison, in small amounts,
is also medicine.

20:00.282 --> 20:01.241
More than anything,

20:01.325 --> 20:04.786
it’s not something that can be dealt
with by just one cup of tea,

20:04.870 --> 20:07.372
and I’m not pregnant.

20:07.456 --> 20:09.208
That’s true.

20:09.291 --> 20:11.668
Besides, this is the kitchen.

20:11.752 --> 20:14.171
It’s not a place for you, Lord Jinshi.

20:14.254 --> 20:16.256
Quit fussing over the details.

20:16.757 --> 20:18.675
What about High Officer Gaoshun?

20:19.343 --> 20:23.138
He's delivering a message.
Could you also give me some tea?

20:23.722 --> 20:25.474
What kind of tea would you like?

20:25.557 --> 20:28.310
- I want the same one as yours.
- That was the last cup.

20:29.061 --> 20:31.855
If you pour more hot water,
it’ll be just be tea from used leaves.

20:31.939 --> 20:33.190
That’s fine.

20:33.690 --> 20:35.442
<i>I can't serve you that.</i>

20:38.278 --> 20:40.239
What other effects does this tea have?

20:40.906 --> 20:42.824
It calms the mind.

20:43.325 --> 20:46.870
It’s also effective for insomnia
and has a refreshing effect.

20:46.954 --> 20:50.165
Other than that, though,
it is not good during pregnancy,

20:50.249 --> 20:53.877
but I’ve heard it can help
induce labor when giving birth.

20:54.544 --> 20:56.463
There's more of a good effect.

20:56.546 --> 21:00.300
Yes, that’s why the side effects
are often overlooked.

21:06.890 --> 21:08.433
It’s white tea.

21:08.517 --> 21:10.102
I said the used leaves were fine.

21:11.853 --> 21:15.565
Speaking of which, jasmine also has
other different benefits.

21:15.649 --> 21:16.566
What kind?

21:16.650 --> 21:20.028
Infertility. Mainly due to the male side.

21:22.823 --> 21:24.241
<i>No, I shouldn't have said that!</i>

21:24.324 --> 21:27.703
<i>Did I go too far with the sarcasm?
Let me get some tea snacks.</i>

21:36.670 --> 21:39.172
I don’t really like it. I’ll leave.

21:41.383 --> 21:42.676
<i>I messed up.</i>

21:48.598 --> 21:49.725
Lord Jinshi.

21:50.309 --> 21:52.978
- Did you get the message out?
- Yes.

21:53.895 --> 21:56.398
And the mid-ranking Lady Jin
has passed away.

21:56.481 --> 21:57.733
Lady Jin?

22:01.987 --> 22:02.821
Poison...?

22:03.864 --> 22:05.198
No way...

23:46.091 --> 23:50.095
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:57.352 --> 24:00.021
<i>The next episode is "Human fungus."</i>

24:00.105 --> 24:00.939
